    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math lessons by adapting to individual learning paces. For example, they can provide step-by-step solutions for common problems, clarify misconceptions, and offer practice problems tailored to a student’s needs. This makes math more accessible and less intimidating for learners."
